id: DRAFT-libbtrfs-dev-6.2-harmonyos-adaptation
trigger_tool: clang|conan|cmake
phase: compilation|linking|testing
error_signature: redefinition of 'btrfs_ioctl_vol_args'|redefinition of 'btrfs_ioctl_search_key'|redefinition of 'btrfs_ioctl_balance_args'
software: libbtrfs-dev
version: 6.2
platform: HarmonyOS PC aarch64
source_tag: v6.2
source_commit: 2f2543b303fea89f78df7a09719d25b595848d0a
pr: 13778
severity: 2
category: dependency, headers, btrfs, portability, upstream-drift
match_keywords: libbtrfs, ioctl.h, btrfs_tree.h, btrfs.h, duplicate ioctl struct, header conflict, HarmonyOS, btrfs-compsize
title: "【知识库扩展】feat(libbtrfs-dev): 6.2 适配 HarmonyOS PC"

root_cause: >
  The legacy public libbtrfs/ioctl.h and libbtrfsutil/btrfs_tree.h with its
  companion btrfs.h expose overlapping ioctl structure definitions. Flattening
  both header sets into include/btrfs makes a consumer that includes ctree.h
  fail with redefinition errors. The package must choose the libbtrfs header
  family required by older consumers and must not install the conflicting
  btrfs_tree.h/btrfs.h pair beside it.

affected_scope: >
  Conan development packages that flatten headers from both legacy libbtrfs
  and libbtrfsutil into a shared include/btrfs directory, including downstream
  consumers of btrfs-progs v6.2 headers.

verification_cmd: >
  Build an external C consumer against the installed Conan package and include
  btrfs/ctree.h, btrfs/ioctl.h and btrfs/send-stream.h together. Then build and
  run the separate HarmonyOS AArch64 LP64/ioctl ABI consumer.

rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: keep-lib-btrfs-header-family-coherent
rec_description: >
  Package the legacy libbtrfs headers and library as one coherent public
  include set; exclude libbtrfsutil/btrfs_tree.h and btrfs.h when they collide
  with legacy ioctl.h definitions. Verify through an external target consumer.
rec_command: "conan create archives/l/libbtrfs-dev/6.2 -pr:h=ohos-aarch64 -pr:b=ohos-aarch64 --build=missing"
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: manual

fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: split-header-namespaces
fallback_description: >
  If an application needs both APIs, install libbtrfsutil UAPI headers in a
  separate include namespace instead of flattening them over legacy headers.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: manual

forbid_1_pattern: "#include.*btrfs_tree.h.*#include.*btrfs/ctree.h|flatten.*btrfs_tree.h.*ioctl.h"
forbid_1_reason: >
  The mixed include set redeclares ioctl structs such as
  btrfs_ioctl_vol_args and btrfs_ioctl_search_key.
forbid_1_consequence: HarmonyOS target consumer compilation fails.
forbid_2_pattern:
forbid_2_reason:
forbid_2_consequence:

